# Build context exclusions for images built from the repo root.
#
# Only the frontend builds this way, because it needs `docs/` — which lives above
# `frontend/` and so is unreachable from a `./frontend` context. The backend images still
# build from `./backend` and use `backend/.dockerignore`; this file does not affect them.
#
# Without this, a root context would ship node_modules, both virtualenvs, the full git
# history and every corpus database to the daemon on each build.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
build
dist
*.egg-info

# Python
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
**/.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Version control and secrets
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Private documentation. Gitignored as "not for publication", so it is absent from a CI
# clone — but present on the author's machine, where it would otherwise be copied into the
# build context and then swept into the standalone bundle by Next's output file tracing.
# `lib/docs.ts` already refuses to generate a route for it; this stops the raw file from
# reaching the image at all, which is the difference between "unreachable" and "not there".
docs/deep-dive/04_Interview_Defense.md

# Runtime data — corpus databases are user content, never image content
data
**/data/corpus
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
logs
*.log

# Test and tooling artifacts
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
.qoder

# Desktop build residue (Rust target dirs are enormous)
desktop/target
desktop/gen

# OS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
